  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8484;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be the greatest integer&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>t</mi></math>, then the number of points, where the function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is not differentiable, is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mtext>Integer</mtext></math></p><p>Now let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sinx</mi></math>, now plotting the diagram of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/48e8d165-bbd6-4d68-97b0-8b669c4ea32f-image.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 311px;\" /></p><p>Now from above diagram we can see that,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sinx</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is not differentiable at intersection points of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>Points of non-differentiability<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
